  "termsLiability": "As section 7 of the MPL 2.0 says, no contributor or distributor of the app is liable to you for any damages of any kind, under any legal theory, whether tort (including negligence), contract, or otherwise. This covers direct, indirect, special, incidental, and consequential damages, including lost profits, lost goodwill, work stoppage, and computer failure or malfunction. It does not limit liability for death or personal injury caused by a party's negligence where the law does not allow such a limit. Some jurisdictions do not allow incidental or consequential damages to be excluded or limited, so this part may not apply to you.",
  "termsIndependentHeading": "Independent Project",
  "termsIndependent": "Libre BM6 is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by the manufacturer of any battery monitor. Libre BM6 is published by Rogue Tinkerer LLC. These terms are between you and the publisher, not the app store you got the app from. The app store is not responsible for the app, for supporting it, or for any claim about it.",
  "termsAccuracyHeading": "Readings May Be Wrong",
  "termsAccuracy": "Readings are for information only and may be inaccurate or delayed. On one tested battery monitor, the voltage read ~0.1 V lower than a multimeter.",
  "termsSafetyHeading": "Safety",
  "termsSafety": "Do not rely on this app for any safety decision. Do not use it while driving. Please check your battery and vehicle with proper tools or a qualified professional. Installing, connecting, or servicing a battery monitor involves electrical and chemical hazards. You do that at your own risk.",
  "termsFullLicenseHeading": "The Full License",
  "termsFullLicense": "The complete text of the MPL 2.0 is available at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/. It governs the software itself. Nothing in these terms restricts any right the MPL 2.0 gives you. If these terms and the MPL 2.0 conflict about the software, the MPL 2.0 governs.",
