  "privacySummaryHeading": "The Short Version",
  "privacySummary": "We treat you and your data the way we want to be treated. There is no account, no ads, and no tracking. Nothing leaves your phone unless you choose to report a bug or ask for support.",
  "privacyStoredHeading": "What the App Stores",
  "privacyStored": "The app stores only the battery monitors you save: each one's Bluetooth identifier and the name you give it. It also remembers that you accepted the Terms of Service. This stays in the app's private storage on your phone. Where the system allows it, the app excludes this from backups. Otherwise, your phone's own backup may include it. Deleting a battery monitor removes it. Uninstalling the app removes everything from your phone.",
  "privacyNotDoneHeading": "What the App Does Not Do",
  "privacyNotDone": "There is no account, sign-in, advertising, analytics, or crash reporting. The app makes no network connections, so it sends nothing off your phone. It does not access your location.",
  "privacyBluetoothHeading": "Bluetooth Permissions",
  "privacyBluetooth": "The app asks for permission to find and connect to nearby Bluetooth devices. It uses that permission only to find your battery monitor and read it. It never uses Bluetooth to work out your location.",
  "privacyBugReportHeading": "Bug Reports and Support",
  "privacyBugReport": "If you tap Report a bug or Contact support, the app opens the project's GitHub page in your browser with a draft. This happens only when you tap one of them. The draft contains only the app version and build number and your phone's operating system version, and you can edit or remove them before you submit. GitHub's own terms and privacy policy apply there. The app itself still makes no network connections.",
  "privacySourceHeading": "Source Code",
  "privacySource": "The app is free software under the Mozilla Public License 2.0, available at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/. Anyone can read its source code to check these statements.",
  "privacyChangesHeading": "Changes",
  "privacyChanges": "This policy may change in a future version of the app. The policy shown in the version you use is the one that applies.",
  "privacyContactHeading": "Contact",
  "privacyContact": "Libre BM6 is published by Rogue Tinkerer LLC. Please ask questions about this policy on the project's issues page at {url}.",
